.docname {Run the Application}
.include {docs}

.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Stack | Every container of CrowdVision running together on one machine | Caddy, Redis, Kafka, the services |
    | Watch | Compose copies a saved file into the running container, or rebuilds it | Edit `src/main.rs`, `telemetry` restarts |
    | Runtime file | `compose.runtime.yml`, written at each start, listing the compose files kept | The input of every `just stack` and `just db` recipe |
    | Exclude | A word that leaves out every folder or service whose name contains it | `simulator` |
    | Detached | Containers run in the background; the terminal is free | `just stack start` |

How to start, look at, reset and stop CrowdVision on one machine, and on the local cluster. First-time setup comes before: [Setting Up the Environment](setting-up.qd). How Compose is wired: [Docker Compose](../toolchain/compose.qd).

---

## Start and stop

| Command | Runs | Files used | Terminal |
|---|---|---|---|
| `just stack dev` | Everything, with watch | each `docker-compose.yml` plus each `docker-compose.dev.yml` | Stays attached |
| `just stack start` | Everything, rebuilt, no watch | each `docker-compose.yml` only | Detached |
| `just stack down` | Stops and removes every container, ignoring any exclusion | the last runtime file | Returns |
| `just stack logs [service]` | Follows the logs, all or one | the last runtime file | Stays attached |

Both `dev` and `start` run `just stack env` first. What `just stack dev` does, step by step: [Docker Compose](../toolchain/compose.qd).

The dev files add, per service: the watch rules, a database port on the host, and a web page to browse the database.

---

## Leaving parts out

| Flag or word | Leaves out |
|---|---|
| `--no-agent` | The `backend/agent` folder: `agent`, `agent-db` and Langfuse |
| `--no-metrics` | `prometheus`, `grafana` |
| `--no-simulators` | `sensor-simulator`, `aq-simulator`, `ap-simulator` |
| `--no-devices` | `ap-collector` |
| Any bare word | Every folder and service whose name contains it |
| `--build` | Nothing: rebuilds the images first |
| `--dry-run` | Nothing: prints the `docker compose` command and stops |

**Example.** `just stack dev --no-simulators frontend`:

- Folders skipped: the three in `simulators/`, and `frontend`.
- The runner prints `excluded: simulators/aq-simulator`, and so on, then the command it runs.
- `ap-collector` still starts: it lives in `devices/`. It finds no simulated router and posts nothing.

.box {A mistyped word is silent} type:{warning}
    A mistyped flag stops the run: `unrecognized arguments: --no-metrcs`. A mistyped word matches nothing, and every service starts. `--dry-run` shows the list before anything starts.

