## Addresses

| Page | Address | When |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend | `http://localhost:8080` | Always |
| Edge, every API | `http://localhost` | Always |
| Keycloak, sign-in and admin console | `http://localhost:8090` | Always |
| Langfuse | `http://localhost:3030`, or `http://localhost/langfuse`, which redirects there | Without `--no-agent` |
| Grafana | `http://localhost/grafana/` | Without `--no-metrics` |
| Prometheus | `http://localhost/prometheus/` | Without `--no-metrics` |
| `digital-twin` database, Mongo Express | `http://localhost/twin-db-gui/` | `dev` only |
| `telemetry` database, pgweb | `http://localhost/telemetry-db-gui/` | `dev` only |
| `notification` database, Mongo Express | `http://localhost/notification-db-gui/` | `dev` only |
| `dashboard` database, Mongo Express | `http://localhost/dashboard-db-gui/` | `dev` only |
| `chat` database, Mongo Express | `http://localhost/chat-db-gui/` | `dev` only |
| Simulators | `localhost:3001` sensor, `:3002` air quality, `:3003` routers | Without `--no-simulators` |

Every database port on the host: [Docker Compose](../toolchain/compose.qd).

---

## Resetting data

| Command | Does |
|---|---|
| `just db clear` | Drops the `chat`, `digital-twin` and `notification` databases. Empties the `agent`'s documents and chunks |
| `just db clear-telemetry` | Empties the `telemetry` tables: readings, thresholds, sensors, rooms, buildings |

- Both act on the last runtime file, so the stack must have been started through `just`.
- The volumes stay. A full wipe is `just stack down`, then `docker volume rm` on the volume.
- `tenancy`, `registry` and Keycloak keep their data: an account and its domains survive both commands.

---

## The local cluster

First creation: [Setting Up the Environment](setting-up.qd). Everything else: [Kubernetes & Istio](../toolchain/kubernetes.qd).

### Running a local change in the cluster

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant D as developer
        participant Dk as docker
        participant K3 as k3d
        participant K as kubectl
        D->>Dk: docker build, tag ghcr.io/nickghignatti/crowdvision-twin:latest
        D->>K3: just k8s load
        K3-->>K3: images copied into the cluster nodes
        D->>K: just k8s restart digital-twin
        K-->>D: new pod with the new image
        D->>K: just k8s rollout digital-twin
        K-->>D: rollout finished

| Step | Command |
|---|---|
| 1 | `docker build -t ghcr.io/nickghignatti/crowdvision-twin:latest -f backend/digital-twin/Dockerfile .` |
| 2 | `just k8s load`: imports all twelve images, so each must exist locally |
| 4 | `just k8s restart digital-twin` |
| 6 | `just k8s rollout digital-twin` |

- Every image builds from the repo root with `-f backend/<service>/Dockerfile .`, except `frontend`, which builds from `./frontend`. The services read sibling folders, such as `backend/libs/` and `schemas/`.
- `just k8s build` builds all twelve. See the gap about Rust images on [Setting Up the Environment](setting-up.qd).

### Day to day

| Command | Does |
|---|---|
| `just k8s stop` | Pauses the cluster. Pods, volumes and secrets stay |
| `just k8s start` | Resumes it |
| `just k8s status` | Lists pods, deployments, services, StatefulSets |
| `just k8s logs digital-twin` | Follows one service's logs |
| `just k8s apply` | Applies every manifest again. Safe to repeat |
| `just k8s restart-all` | Restarts every deployment, after a secret changes |
| `just k8s delete` | Deletes the `crowdvision` namespace and all its data. The cluster stays |
| `k3d cluster delete crowdvision` | Deletes the cluster itself |

---

## When something goes wrong

| What is seen | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `502` from `localhost` | Caddy reached a service that is not listening yet, or crashed | `just stack logs <service>`. A Rust service compiles for minutes on the first start |
| A left-out service starts anyway | The word was mistyped | `--dry-run`, or the flag |
| `compose.runtime.yml not found` | No `just stack` run started this stack | Start it with `just stack dev` |
| A new variable is empty | `.env` predates it | `just stack env`: it adds only what is missing |
| `just k8s secrets`: namespaces not found | The namespace does not exist yet | `kubectl apply -f k8s/namespace.yml`, then again |
| Pods in `ImagePullBackOff` | The cluster tries to pull an image it does not have | Build it, then `just k8s load` |
| Windows: `kubectl` cannot connect after `just k8s start` | The load balancer came back on another port | `docker ps --filter name=k3d-crowdvision-serverlb`, then `kubectl config set-cluster k3d-crowdvision --server=https://127.0.0.1:<port>` |
| Sign-in fails in the cluster | Keycloak is not deployed there | Point `claims-gateway` at a reachable Keycloak |

